 * great many untranslated entries, and carrying those would add bytes to produce exactly what the
 * English fallback already produces.
 *
 * Consulted only when the platform returns nothing, so a platform that has its own name keeps it.
 * Assembled from what the platforms collectively know: their gaps barely overlap, so between them
 * they cover nearly every pair this library ships. The exception is a display language with no
 * CLDR data anywhere, such as Halkomelem or Mohawk: almost nothing can name a locale in it, and those pairs
 * are absent here and fall back to English.
 *
 * Generated from Unicode CLDR 48.2.0, with names for pairs CLDR lacks taken from platform CLDR
 * implementations. Do not edit by hand — regenerate with the procedure in
 * `docs/knowledge/guides/regenerating-display-name-tables.md`, which collects from every platform
 * because no single one of them can fill its own gaps.
 *
 * Packed as one string per display language rather than 4683 separate entries: the payload is the
 * same, and Kotlin/Native compiles a handful of large literals far more happily than thousands of
 * small declarations. Each blob is `tag\u0001name\u0001tag\u0001name…`, sorted by tag, and is
 * parsed on first use for that language only.
 */
